{"kind":"report","text":"Decision for85680f62: proceed with an explicitly selected isolated-object mode, with the framing and allowance requirements below. This is a bounded G0 transport design decision; it approves no actual host support, source candidate, publication, first-head replacement, G1 or complete e029 outcome.\n\nProtocol basis: Git's pack negotiation permits deepen plus filter, and explicitly wanted objects survive the filter. tree depth0 omits unrequested trees/blobs. That supports this candidate for commit/root/affected-path retrieval, subject to actual server behavior. https://git-scm.com/docs/gitprotocol-pack ; https://git-scm.com/docs/git-rev-list . These are documentary premises, not a provider observation.\n\n1. Keep default full-closure mode and existing callers unchanged. Select isolation explicitly and keep its partial cache/facts distinct from any known-complete base/closure state. Require the server's shallow/filter capabilities and the applicable permission for a nonadvertised want before POST. Capability advertisement permits the request, not a claim that every requested object/filter combination is accepted. In particular, allow-tip alone is not evidence of arbitrary non-tip tree/blob access. Actual denial is unreadable/unsupported, never proof of object absence. Preserve format, complete advertisement, origin/redirect/authentication and HTTP media checks. https://git-scm.com/docs/gitprotocol-capabilities .\n\n2. For the current no-have/non-sideband flow, request one want with selected advertised capabilities, deepen1, filter tree:0, flush, then done. Parse the positive-depth shallow-update phase BEFORE NAK/pack. The phase may legally contain ZERO shallow lines followed by flush: a root commit and noncommit wants must not require a nonempty boundary. Accept bounded correctly shaped boundary data only; no unshallow line is legitimate when the client supplied no prior shallow set. Validate any returned boundary against the one wanted commit after decoding; do not treat it as ancestry/closure evidence. Missing flush, unexpected ACK/ERR/framing, malformed/duplicate/unrelated boundary or trailing data refuse. Keep thin-pack/sideband/multi-ack unsupported unless separately implemented and tested.\n\n3. Exact-one-object is the explicit success contract, not an assumption about what every conforming host sends. Bound the pack header object count to1 BEFORE inflation/retention in this mode, then check the sole verified object is the exact wanted ID and its required type/size. A self-contained one-object pack needs no external delta base. Refuse extra objects, missing want and denied filter behavior without retrying an unfiltered/full pack. If annotated-tag wants cannot meet that contract, expose the supported object-kind envelope truthfully; keep their old full-mode behavior. GitSource.object currently has no expected-type argument: its caller's Reader must still verify expected type/hash, or the isolated interface must bind that explicitly. Do not label unverified envelope metadata as a verified object.\n\n4. Charge wire request/advertisement/response, pkt-line/boundary counts, inflated bytes, cache, output copies and object count against explicit budgets BEFORE the corresponding allocation/work. Apply the caller's requested object allowance before inflating an over-limit single body, not only to the final return copy. Budget existing cache plus in-flight wire/concat/pack/decompression/delta/output copies; maxBytes checked independently at each stage is not one aggregate-memory bound. Serialize fetch/decode operations per source or reserve their simultaneous working allowance, including cache-hit output copies. Do not admit many concurrent operations on the strength of the same free cache bytes. Caller-owned retained path objects also need an operation-wide byte/object/deadline budget. State what the code bounds and account for engine/stream overhead separately; measured peak memory remains a separate witness.\n\n5. Use actual local upload-pack for advertised commit, reachable nonadvertised tree/blob and root/no-parent/empty-shallow cases. Label any HTTP adapter stand-in. Instrument bytes/objects/POSTs so long unrelated ancestry and a large unrelated blob are not transferred or decoded. Remove a required capability and show refusal before POST; exercise a host ignoring filters, wrong/missing object, malformed boundary, over-budget compressed/inflated data and concurrent allowance pressure. Preserve full-mode compatibility and ordinary closure witnesses. A focused distinguishing control and one final source gate suffice; no sweep, whole-suite repetition or production probe.\n\nStatic basis: exact current Maine987350d Git reader/transport files are byte-identical to inspected0157307b9 versions. SmartHttpSource419-440 currently fetches/caches a full decoded pack before applying the return allowance; decodePack241-320 separately bounds wire/inflated/constructed bytes and allocates several owned representations. The new mode must address those allocations, not merely its final map. The separate affected-path editor may consume verified objects and preserve untouched names/modes/IDs, but it proves only the objects actually read. All current closure, checker-snapshot and ancestry duties, and G1 retained-base possession/own-answer publication contracts remain intact. No project tests, gate, source edits or provider operation was run for this decision.","body":{"formal_source_approval":"false","review_scope":"pre-Source transport design","source_baseline":"e987350d3031ed7f5ee707874f24671734a84d49"}}